lee-texparts.js, lee-board.js, lee-board.css, board/rough.js and board/perfect-freehand.mjs: the screen guide's formula parts and board, copied unchanged from abhyasa main, commit 08fe6d7, which is released as abhyasa 0.0.16, wheel abhyasa-0.0.16-py3-none-any.whl, SHA-256 TODO. TODO at release: put the wheel's SHA-256 and its download URL here, check the five digests below against the files in the wheel, and move the pin in pyproject.toml to abhyasa==0.0.16. Until then, test_abhyasa_is_pinned_to_the_vendored_wheel and test_readme_records_the_digest_of_the_wheel fail, and test_vendored_files_equal_the_installed_wheel fails against the 0.0.15 pin. The source files are abhyasa/core/texparts.js, abhyasa/core/board.js, abhyasa/core/board.css, abhyasa/core/vendor/rough.js and abhyasa/core/vendor/perfect-freehand.mjs. tests/test_vendor_board.py compares each file with the file in the installed abhyasa. board/ is the folder the page passes to the board as `host.assets`, served at /leestatic/board/. board/LICENSES.md is abhyasa's licence file for the two libraries. Before the release, copy the files from a clean checkout of that commit:

    a=<abhyasa checkout> && for f in texparts.js:lee-texparts.js board.js:lee-board.js board.css:lee-board.css vendor/rough.js:board/rough.js vendor/perfect-freehand.mjs:board/perfect-freehand.mjs vendor/LICENSES.md:board/LICENSES.md; do git -C "$a" show "08fe6d7:abhyasa/core/${f%%:*}" > "leela/vendor/${f##*:}"; done

After the release, download the wheel into an empty folder, check the digest, extract it into another folder, then copy the files:

    d=$(mktemp -d) && curl -sS -o "$d/abhyasa-0.0.16-py3-none-any.whl" <URL TODO> && shasum -a 256 "$d/abhyasa-0.0.16-py3-none-any.whl"
    e=$(mktemp -d) && unzip -q "$d/abhyasa-0.0.16-py3-none-any.whl" -d "$e" && c="$e/abhyasa/core" && cp "$c/texparts.js" leela/vendor/lee-texparts.js && cp "$c/board.js" leela/vendor/lee-board.js && cp "$c/board.css" leela/vendor/lee-board.css && cp "$c/vendor/rough.js" "$c/vendor/perfect-freehand.mjs" "$c/vendor/LICENSES.md" leela/vendor/board/

The board's paper uses the hand font Patrick Hand (OFL). It is not copied: Leela serves rupaka's font files and their `@font-face` rules (`rupaka.render.font_css`) at /leefonts/, from the rupaka that pyproject.toml pins, as abhyasa serves /assets/hand.css.

